  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "REVIEW_LOCAL",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "e4d4cfe94953fa36fdeed9fee5b94081916b355629fb3341ac0f14b1cb39de44"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For the cubic-etale rank-two self-adjoint data of theorem.md Section 1 with a B-self-dual lattice L and Q_1(L) integral, Theorem A reproduces the literal intrinsic shell lemma at every prime and depth. Theorem B has odd-prime sup norm vol(R), support p^(-c) h d^(-1) for c>0, the one-step boundary support and 8 vol(R) product q^(-1/2) for c=0 at every odd prime, and dyadic support 2^(-max(c+3,4)) h d^(-1). These are prose mathematical conclusions, not kernel or downstream global certification.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "93f0d10950bfd5a3d59164d398e1e5fd1daac6e6b533d80bf13ea6ff6a813976"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "REVIEW_SHARPNESS",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "e4d4cfe94953fa36fdeed9fee5b94081916b355629fb3341ac0f14b1cb39de44"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For every prime p, k>=1, c>=2, the split construction in theorem.md Section 6 has actual stabilizer C={(a1,a2,a3) in Z_p^3: a1-a2 in p^(k+c) Z_p}, h=(p^k,p^k,1), and g=c. For every epsilon in Z_p its kernel at (p^(k-c),-p^(k-c),epsilon) equals (1-p^(-1))^2 p^(-c)>0. It proves sharpness of the odd-prime support exponent c, including fully nonzero outputs when epsilon=1, not optimality of the dyadic additive constant.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "26a31548bb3e2c2f9d24ac74cf660f1afff04308594d029fc863e9941cec0060"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "REVIEW_PROFILE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX_DRAFT_REVIEW",
        "content_hash": "e4d4cfe94953fa36fdeed9fee5b94081916b355629fb3341ac0f14b1cb39de44"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For F a cubic number field with E_p=F tensor Q_p, finite S, the local data above, and nonzero z in F integral outside S with nonzero product of local shell kernels, H <= 2^12 |Norm z| D_F G_exp^3 T_boundary and a common containing fractional ideal has inverse norm <= 2^12 D_F G_exp^3, where G_exp=product p^c<=G_0 and boundary includes odd c=0 primes. With boundary restricted to the manuscript convention g=0,p>5, both constants can be 2^12*3^3*5^3, improving only the two profile inequalities from exponent 24 to 3.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "3db7cb6a8d3d222a83093d01fa3da04c3fb319288085002235c2704ddf2db710"
    },
    {
